# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Per-machine tool state (defn AI-native code database)
.defn/

# Per-clone redaction-audit config — patterns are local, never published
.lexicon/

# Secrets — also gitignored under render/.gitignore but belt-and-suspenders
*.env
*.env.local
.env

# Logs / per-machine session state
*.log
session-log.jsonl

# Reference PDFs / EPUBs — large binaries, often copyrighted source
# materials. Kept local-only; never committed (especially never published).
# Note: V8 commit 71710ed historically added 8 PDFs before this rule;
# those remain in git history but no remote is configured, so they
# have not been published.
refs/
render/viz/

# .claude/* ignores everything in .claude/ EXCEPT subdirs we explicitly
# re-include below. (A bare `.claude/` would exclude the dir and make
# negation impossible per gitignore semantics.)
.claude/*
# Project-level skills SHIP with the repo (2026 Claude Code skills
# best practice: skills live at .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md and are
# checked in for everyone working on the project).
!.claude/skills/
.plancheck-debug.json

# Per-session handoff archive — local recovery state, not for the public repo.
# Future handoffs go to .session-handoffs/SESSION-N-HANDOFF.md (V114 d).
.session-handoffs/

# Pre-V114-d top-level handoff/report files (now archived in git history).
SESSION-*.md

# Working procurement queues — transient, format unstable, kept on disk only.
wanted-materials.md
wanted-materials-archive-*.md
mining-queue.md
acquired-materials.md
lexicon.db
lexicon.db-shm
lexicon.db-wal
docs/working/
docs/passes/
__pycache__/

# Batch-sweep and quote-verification audit logs — raw process artifacts, same
# class as docs/passes/. The triage/adjudication .txt files name files from
# refs/ (305 distinct filenames across the directory as of 2026-08-19) —
# exactly the corpus-inventory leak scripts/private/ was gitignored for above.
docs/audits/

# Local utility scripts and config — kept on disk per clone, not shipped.
# Anything that scrapes/fetches external sites stays local-only.
# Tooling is public by default; anything that names how the corpus was
# obtained lives here instead. clean-names.sh hardcoded 29 acquisition
# filenames with publisher metadata, ISBNs and 28 MD5 hashes — an inventory of
# a private corpus plus its provenance — and was the one file the 2026-05-31
# citation scrub never opened, because that pass cleaned the citations where
# the rule is written down and not the tool that implements it.
scripts/private/
scripts/*-fetch.sh
scripts/*-scrape.*
.lexicon/

# Built Pages output (baked by .github/workflows/pages.yml). Anchored to
# repo root — an unanchored `public/` also matched web/public/, Vite's
# legitimate source-asset dir (favicon, icons), not a generated artifact.
/public/

# OCR sidecars and extraction caches — derived from refs/, never committed
.cache/
refs/*.ocr.txt
.ocr-tmp/
**/.ocr-tmp/

# Local ref-resolution pins for scripts/verify-quotes.py. Maps a citation
# slug to the file in refs/ that holds the work. refs/ is a local corpus and
# these filenames carry acquisition formats, so the map stays out of the
# published repo the same way the corpus does.
.refs-pins.tsv
